    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0266" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.20/36b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-18T12:00:00-04:00">March 18,
                            1943—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>986. From the Under Secretary. Please express to Aranha<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d220-f1"/> my confident belief that he will share with me a feeling
                    of approval and gratification at the action of the Governor of French Guiana in
                    placing his Government at the side of the United Nations through his adherence
                    to General Giraud, a step which clearly expresses the will of the people of this
                    French colony. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="31" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
